# 33. TRANSACTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Any operation that changes multiple related states must be transactional where appropriate.

At minimum inspect:

```text
createBooking()
ownerRejectBooking()
assignDriver()
startTrip()
completeTrip()
cancelBooking()
vehicle replacement/status operations where multiple records are affected
```

For example:

```java
@Transactional
```

must be used where Booking + Vehicle + Driver changes must succeed or fail together.

The database must not be left in an inconsistent state such as:

```text
Booking = IN_PROGRESS
Vehicle = AVAILABLE
Driver = ACTIVE
```

or:

```text
Booking = COMPLETED
Vehicle = ON_TRIP
Driver = ON_TRIP
```

when the operation was supposed to complete the trip.

