# 42. ABSOLUTE RULES

These rules have priority throughout the implementation:

1. **Do not invent business rules.**
2. **Existing SRS is the source of truth.**
3. **Approval status and operational status are separate concepts.**
4. **Do not duplicate ****`PENDING`****, ****`APPROVED`****, or ****`REJECTED`**** inside DriverStatus or VehicleStatus.**
5. **Do not introduce ****`OFFLINE`**** into DriverStatus.**
6. **Only Owner can accept/reject bookings.**
7. **Owner acceptance does not equal confirmation.**
8. **Booking becomes CONFIRMED only after required driver assignment or valid owner-as-driver verification.**
9. **Vehicle becomes BOOKED immediately when a customer creates a booking.**
10. **Vehicle Browse requires ****`approvalStatus=APPROVED AND status=AVAILABLE`****.**
11. **Driver assignment requires an approved, operationally available driver.**
12. **Driver becomes ON_TRIP only when the trip actually starts.**
13. **Vehicle becomes ON_TRIP only when the trip actually starts.**
14. **Vehicle and Driver are released only when the applicable business flow completes/releases them.**
15. **Do not introduce date-overlap availability logic unless already required by the SRS.**
16. **Do not reintroduce ****`dailyRate`**** or ****`transmission`****.**
17. **Do not rewrite unrelated modules.**
18. **Do not create duplicate enums.**
19. **Do not rely only on frontend validation.**
20. **Use service-level validation and transactions for important state changes.**
21. **If existing code conflicts with this specification, prioritize this specification and clearly report the conflict.**
22. **If the SRS does not define a behavior, do not silently invent one.**
